{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And El, His hand</b> — it is a future-tense verb in place of past. The proof: <i>ואביא את הלוים</i> [and I will bring the Levites — no, rather:] <i>וידו אבן בי</i> [and His hand was a stone upon me]. It is also possible for it to be past, only it would be of the hif'il pattern. And behold, we find <i>לידות</i>, which indicates the softness [rafaḥ] of the he." "<b>And they gave</b> — the Israelite boy for the price of a prostitute, in exchange for prostitution." "<b>And the girl they sold for wine</b> — for the price of wine to get drunk with the prostitute. For every 'prostitute' [zonah] in Scripture is in its literal sense, except for <i>והזונות רחצו</i> [and the prostitutes washed], which is like <i>אזניך</i>, because the alef is added."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The verse text and the proof citation are textually difficult; the first proof citation <i>ואביא את הלוים</i> appears misplaced or corrupt, and 'עלומי הה\"א' is obscure, rendered hyper-literally as 'softness of the he.'", 2 "The comparison of והזונות to אזניך (with alef added) is cryptic; rendered hyper-literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:44.840401099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}